---
export const prerender = true;
import '../../../styles/global.css';
import '../../../styles/cai-doc.css';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow" />
  <title>Cultivated AI · Mission Control · What to bring · The Baker's Dozen</title>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="cd-shell" style="--doc-accent: var(--color-sky);">

    <div class="cd-printhint screen-only">
      <span class="accent">Send or print →</span>
      Share with the cohort and the data team a week before Session 1. Access takes the longest, so start it early.
    </div>

    <p class="cd-eyebrow">Cultivated AI · Mission Control · what to bring</p>
    <h1 class="cd-title">Come ready to <em>build</em>.</h1>
    <p class="cd-lede">Mission Control builds with your real data, so the setup is heavier than a normal workshop and most of it is about <strong>access</strong>. Sort it a week ahead. If the data isn't reachable, Session 1 turns into a logins meeting.</p>
    <p class="cd-meta">Per cohort · start ~1 week ahead · The Baker's Dozen</p>
    <div class="cd-rule"></div>

    <!-- 01 people -->
    <section class="cd-section" style="--bar: var(--color-sky);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head"><span class="cd-section-num">01</span><h2 class="cd-section-name">The right people <em>in the room</em></h2></div>
      <p class="cd-section-blurb">Decisions get made live (warehouse choice, metric definitions, owners). The people who can make them have to be present.</p>
      <ul class="cd-checklist">
        <li class="cd-check" style="--bar: var(--color-sky);">
          <span class="cd-check-box"></span>
          <div class="cd-check-body"><h4>The leaders who ask the questions</h4><p>The people who actually need answers from the data to make decisions. This is built for them.</p></div>
          <span class="cd-pill" style="--pill: var(--color-amber);">Required</span>
        </li>
        <li class="cd-check" style="--bar: var(--color-purple);">
          <span class="cd-check-box"></span>
          <div class="cd-check-body"><h4>Whoever owns the data</h4><p>The analyst, BI lead, or engineer who maintains Power BI and pulls reports today. They make the build real and can arrange access.</p></div>
          <span class="cd-pill" style="--pill: var(--color-amber);">Required</span>
        </li>
        <li class="cd-check" style="--bar: var(--color-teal);">
          <span class="cd-check-box"></span>
          <div class="cd-check-body"><h4>Someone who can say yes</h4><p>A decision-maker who can approve a warehouse direction and name owners, so the roadmap in Session 4 is real, not a wish list.</p></div>
          <span class="cd-pill" style="--pill: var(--color-teal);">Recommended</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 access -->
    <section class="cd-section" style="--bar: var(--color-purple);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head"><span class="cd-section-num">02</span><h2 class="cd-section-name">Data <em>access</em></h2></div>
      <p class="cd-section-blurb">The one thing that, if missing, stalls everything. Read access is enough; we're not changing anything in your systems.</p>
      <ul class="cd-checklist">
        <li class="cd-check" style="--bar: var(--color-sky);">
          <span class="cd-check-box"></span>
          <div class="cd-check-body"><h4>Power BI, read access</h4><p>Access to the existing reports and the underlying datasets / semantic models, not just the published dashboards.</p></div>
          <span class="cd-pill" style="--pill: var(--color-amber);">Required</span>
        </li>
        <li class="cd-check" style="--bar: var(--color-teal);">
          <span class="cd-check-box"></span>
          <div class="cd-check-body"><h4>GobbleCube exports</h4><p>A way to get the city, store, and platform analytics out (an export, an API key, or a sample file). Bring a recent sample to Session 1.</p></div>
          <span class="cd-pill" style="--pill: var(--color-amber);">Required</span>
        </li>
        <li class="cd-check" style="--bar: var(--color-amber);">
          <span class="cd-check-box"></span>
          <div class="cd-check-body"><h4>Production and supply-chain files</h4><p>Recent samples of whatever you want to plug in (spreadsheets, ERP exports). Anonymise anything sensitive first.</p></div>
          <span class="cd-pill" style="--pill: var(--color-teal);">Recommended</span>
        </li>
        <li class="cd-check" style="--bar: var(--color-navy);">
          <span class="cd-check-box"></span>
          <div class="cd-check-body"><h4>An admin on standby</h4><p>Someone who can grant access or approve a connection during the session if we hit a wall. A name and a Slack away is enough.</p></div>
          <span class="cd-pill" style="--pill: var(--color-teal);">Recommended</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 accounts & tools -->
    <section class="cd-section" style="--bar: var(--color-teal);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head"><span class="cd-section-num">03</span><h2 class="cd-section-name">Accounts and <em>tools</em></h2></div>
      <ul class="cd-checklist">
        <li class="cd-check" style="--bar: var(--color-sky);">
          <span class="cd-check-box"></span>
          <div class="cd-check-body"><h4>A laptop and Google Chrome</h4><p>Mac or Windows. Chrome installed for the querying and AEO exercises.</p></div>
          <span class="cd-pill" style="--pill: var(--color-amber);">Required</span>
        </li>
        <li class="cd-check" style="--bar: var(--color-purple);">
          <span class="cd-check-box"></span>
          <div class="cd-check-body"><h4>An AI account (Claude, ChatGPT, or Gemini)</h4><p>Paid is ideal for the heavier querying, the free tier works. We'll also use a couple of assistants side by side for the AI-answer exercise in Session 4.</p></div>
          <span class="cd-pill" style="--pill: var(--color-amber);">Required</span>
        </li>
        <li class="cd-check" style="--bar: var(--color-amber);">
          <span class="cd-check-box"></span>
          <div class="cd-check-body"><h4>Power BI Copilot, if you have it</h4><p>If Copilot in Fabric / Power BI is already on your plan, have it enabled. It's the fastest way to try the chat layer on existing data. Not required; we can demo it.</p></div>
          <span class="cd-pill" style="--pill: var(--color-teal);">Recommended</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 04 bring -->
    <section class="cd-section" style="--bar: var(--color-amber);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head"><span class="cd-section-num">04</span><h2 class="cd-section-name">Bring to <em>Session 1</em></h2></div>
      <ul class="cd-checklist">
        <li class="cd-check" style="--bar: var(--color-sky);">
          <span class="cd-check-box"></span>
          <div class="cd-check-body"><h4>Your questionnaire answers</h4><p>Especially the five questions you'd ask your data every week, and your one high-impact problem.</p></div>
          <span class="cd-pill" style="--pill: var(--color-amber);">Required</span>
        </li>
        <li class="cd-check" style="--bar: var(--color-teal);">
          <span class="cd-check-box"></span>
          <div class="cd-check-body"><h4>Sample exports from each source</h4><p>A few recent rows from Power BI, GobbleCube, and the production / supply-chain files, so we can map them for real in the room.</p></div>
          <span class="cd-pill" style="--pill: var(--color-teal);">Recommended</span>
        </li>
        <li class="cd-check" style="--bar: var(--color-purple);">
          <span class="cd-check-box"></span>
          <div class="cd-check-body"><h4>The result of the AI-answer check</h4><p>What ChatGPT or Gemini said when you asked "best [your category] in India." A screenshot is perfect.</p></div>
          <span class="cd-pill" style="--pill: var(--color-teal);">Recommended</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 not needed -->
    <section class="cd-section" style="--bar: var(--color-navy);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head"><span class="cd-section-num">05</span><h2 class="cd-section-name">What you <em>don't</em> need</h2></div>
      <div class="cd-prose">
        <p>You don't need a warehouse already built, a data scientist, or any new software bought in advance. You don't need to have cleaned your data first; finding the mess is part of Session 1. Bring the access and the real questions. We build the rest together.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="cd-footer">
      <span class="brand">Cultivated AI · <em>Grow, don't Chase.</em></span>
      <span>Mission Control · prerequisites</span>
    </div>

  </div>
</body>
</html>
